<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eyre Coote</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1726–1783</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Eyre Coote was an Irish-born British army officer who served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. He commanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>'s forces at the Battle of Wandiwash in 1760, which broke French power in southern India, and returned as commander-in-chief in India in 1779. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-mysore-war">Second Anglo-Mysore War</a> he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a> Novo in 1781, and he died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a> in 1783.</p></div>
